    <name>
      <text>sum-geometric-series-i-q3</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A learner posts a short drama video on the school's online page. The numbers of new views on the first three days are:</p>
<p>\({@t1@}, \; {@t2@}, \; {@t3@}, \; \ldots\)</p>

<p>(a) Find the common ratio, \(r\).</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p>(b) Find the total number of views in the first {@m@} days.</p>
<p>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>

<p>(c) The total number of views reaches exactly {@target@} after some days. Find the number of days.</p>
<p>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>

<p>(d) After how many days does the total number of views first become more than {@cap@}?</p>
<p>[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The numbers of new views are {@t1@}, {@t2@}, {@t3@}, ... This is a geometric progression (GP).</p>

<p>(a) <strong>Common ratio:</strong></p>
<p>\[ r = \frac{ {@t2@} }{ {@t1@} } = {@ta1@} \]</p>

<p>(b) <strong>Total for the first {@m@} days:</strong></p>
<p>\[ S_{ {@m@} } = \frac{ {@a@}\left({@r@}^{ {@m@} } - 1\right)}{ {@r@} - 1 } = \frac{ {@a@} \times {@r^m - 1@} }{ {@r - 1@} } = {@ta2@} \]</p>

<p>(c) <strong>Number of days for a total of {@target@}:</strong></p>
<p>Put \( S_n = {@target@} \), \( a = {@a@} \) and \( r = {@r@} \) into the formula:</p>
<p>\[ \frac{ {@a@}\left({@r@}^{n} - 1\right)}{ {@r - 1@} } = {@target@} \]</p>
<p>Solve for \( {@r@}^{n} - 1 \):</p>
<p>\[ {@r@}^{n} - 1 = {@target*(r-1)/a@} \]</p>
<p>\[ {@r@}^{n} = {@Rt@} \]</p>
<p>Write {@Rt@} as a power of {@r@}:</p>
<p>\[ {@r@}^{ {@k@} } = {@Rt@} \]</p>
<p>So \( n = {@ta3@} \). The total reaches {@target@} after {@ta3@} days.</p>

<p>(d) <strong>First day with a total of more than {@cap@}:</strong></p>
<p>We need \( S_n > {@cap@} \):</p>
<p>\[ \frac{ {@a@}\left({@r@}^{n} - 1\right)}{ {@r - 1@} } > {@cap@} \]</p>
<p>Solve for \( {@r@}^{n} \):</p>
<p>\[ {@r@}^{n} - 1 > {@Rq - 1@} \]</p>
<p>\[ {@r@}^{n} > {@Rq@} \]</p>
<p>The unknown \(n\) is in the power, so take logarithms of both sides:</p>
<p>\[ n \log {@r@} > \log {@Rq@} \]</p>
<p>\[ n > \frac{\log {@Rq@}}{\log {@r@}} = {@n_disp@} \]</p>
<p>\(n\) must be a whole number of days. The smallest whole number bigger than {@n_disp@} is {@ta4@}.</p>
<p>So the total number of views first becomes more than {@cap@} after {@ta4@} days.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
